  "visual_review": "Viewed both newly generated 20-panel material contact sheets and the three-way close-up comparison. All 18 expected equipment scenes are present. Native emission visibly brightens the five tool heads, held Hardened Glowstone items and each individually worn armor piece compared with the matching zero-alpha scenes; armor emission retains visible seam/mask patterns and tool silhouettes. The placed Hardened Glowstone face is brighter than ordinary Glowstone and its zero-alpha control. Its diffuse texture is a simple gold face with a border, confirmed by viewing the unchanged source PNG; the native close-up keeps that border and face geometry despite strong bloom. Close-up code-value ratios are 1.20071 against ordinary and 1.25099 against zero-alpha; all 15 required held/worn ratios exceed one, minimum 1.11808. All four distance assertions are retained in the separate current, reviewed companion-on profile. Actual report hashes, byte-identical production classes, matched backend/shader/settings and the whole-ZIP thirteen-alpha-only change were authenticated. Startup GL diagnostics remain recorded and do not establish warning-free OptiFine compatibility."
